much feverish activity, a great deal of get-up-and-go, but no
one seems ş where he is going.
Everything has a purpose, or ¤. Every second of our
life has its own ¤, whether or not ă conscious of it
¯ time. That ¤ ú as simple as breathing or as
complex as a vital emotional decision, but it is always there.
We may not succeed in proving each tiny ¤, but that
