through lack of sustenance. And ń brought about × pas-
sage ¦ mesaraic veins becoming continually restricted ×
thickening ¡ skin ¡se veins [hardening ¡ arteries—
L.E.]: ª process continues until it affects the capillary veins
which are ä to close up altogether; and from this it comes
to pass ´ old dread the cold more than the young, and that
those who are very old have their sk£ color of wood or of dried
chestnut, because ń almost completely deprived of sustenance.
Here, too, transition works stealthily. The arteries are
